Atlas overlay patch 0104: ui/kit-layout-provider
Why: dialogs, sheets and bubbles take the Design System's numbers when the Kit chrome is on (ADR 0062): the dialog
inset 16 (sheet.toml), the buttons 8 px apart (sheet.toml) and padded 12 (button.toml). ChromeLayoutProvider asks
atlas::kit::KitInsetsMetric / KitDistanceMetric first and uses the engine's value when they answer nothing; the
numbers are in chrome/browser/ui/atlas/kit/kit_metrics.h and atlas/transform/kit_metrics.py --check holds them to
the design repo's specs. Radii need no hook: patch 0070 already makes them the Design System's. The dependency is the
small //chrome/browser/ui/atlas/kit:metrics target (no cycle with the views).
Files: chrome/browser/ui/views/chrome_layout_provider.cc, chrome/browser/ui/views/BUILD.gn
Test filter: *AtlasKitMetrics*
Rebase risk: L (one include, two early returns, one dep line)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

